Exit when the editor cannot bind its listener

Report any listener error raised before the server is listening as a failed
server process, so the bootstrap and watchdog can retry and the gave-up page
can show the reason. The listener is a private socket now, and a full disk, a
refused path or a read-only directory fail the bind as surely as a busy port
did, leaving a process that serves nothing and that nothing replaces. Errors
after listening retain the existing remote service handler.

--- a/src/server-main.ts
+++ b/src/server-main.ts
@@ -106,6 +106,10 @@
 		return remoteExtensionHostAgentServer.handleUpgrade(req, socket);
 	});
 	server.on('error', async (err) => {
+		if (!server.listening) {
+			console.error('Editor failed to bind its port', err);
+			process.exit(1);
+		}
 		const remoteExtensionHostAgentServer = await getRemoteExtensionHostAgentServer();
 		return remoteExtensionHostAgentServer.handleServerError(err);
 	});
